			"notes": "## ⚠️ Before you update\n\n2.0.0 changes the database. **Stop every server that shares the database, update them all, then start them.** On the first start the 1.x tables are renamed to `judicator_*` (with their rows) and players are identified by UUID everywhere; a 1.x server no longer finds the tables after that. The *Upgrading to 2.0.0* section of the [README](https://github.com/oleonardosilva/judicator/blob/v2.0.0/README.md) lists every change to tables, commands and the API.\n\n## 📦 Which file?\n\n| Platform | File | Requirements |\n|---|---|---|\n| Velocity (proxy) | `Judicator-Velocity-2.0.0.jar` | Velocity 3.4+, Java 17+ |\n| BungeeCord (proxy) | `Judicator-BungeeCord-2.0.0.jar` | BungeeCord 1.21+, Java 17+ |\n| Spigot / Paper / Folia | `Judicator-Bukkit-2.0.0.jar` | Minecraft 1.8.8+ (Folia 1.20.1+), Java 17+ |\n| Fabric (server mod) | `Judicator-Fabric-2.0.0.jar` | Minecraft 26.1+, Java 25, Fabric API |\n| NeoForge (server mod) | `Judicator-NeoForge-2.0.0.jar` | Minecraft 26.1+, Java 25 |\n| Forge (server mod) | `Judicator-Forge-2.0.0.jar` | Minecraft 26.1+, Java 25, Forge 62+ |\n| Hytale (**experimental**) | `Judicator-Hytale-2.0.0.jar` | Hytale server 0.7.4+, Java 25 |\n| Developers | `judicator-api-2.0.0.jar` (+ sources, javadoc) | compile against it, do not shade it |\n\nRunning a network? Install the proxy build on Velocity/BungeeCord; see *Networks and Multiple Servers* in the README for the backends. `SHA256SUMS.txt` has the checksum of every file.\n\n## 🛠️ Changelog\n\n### 🌐 Platforms\n* New: BungeeCord, Spigot/Paper from 1.8.8 to the latest, Folia, Fabric, NeoForge and Forge (Minecraft 26.1+), and an **experimental** Hytale plugin (compiled against the server API, not yet run on a server).\n* SQLite is the default database, no setup needed; MySQL/MariaDB and PostgreSQL are still supported.\n* Runtime libraries are downloaded from Maven Central and checked against a fixed SHA-256.\n\n### 🖱️ Menus\n* `/jmenu`: everything the commands show, in menus: bans and mutes in force, reports, players online, a player's page with their history, warns, notes and linked accounts, and every action behind a confirmation.\n* Lists with order, filters and search.\n* On Paper, players on 1.21.6+ get the game's own dialogs: reasons and notes typed in text fields instead of the chat, the way out always apart from the actions.\n* `menus.replace-commands`: the lookup commands open the menu for players.\n\n### 🛡️ Moderation\n* Player reports: `/report` and `/reports` (assign, close, teleport).\n* Server and group scopes for bans and mutes; cross-server sync and proxy mode for backends.\n* Staff hierarchy, time limits per group, cooldowns.\n* Silent and progressive punishments; preset reasons with their own menu icons.\n* `/unban`, `/unmute`, `/extend`, `/changereason`, staff rollback, staff notes, `/playerinfo`.\n* Soft mutes and mutes that only count online time; exemptions, IP limits and ban evasion checks.\n* Data retention and per-player language.\n* `/blame`, `/activity`, `/banlist`, `/mutelist` and `/judicator help` by category.\n* Import punishments from other ban plugins, from vanilla, or from another Judicator database (`/judicator import`).\n\n### 🌍 Languages\n* Messages in English, Spanish, Portuguese, French and German; with `per-player-language: true` each player gets their game's language.\n\n### 🔌 Integrations\n* PlaceholderAPI placeholders (Spigot/Paper), a public API with events, bStats metrics, Discord webhooks for reports.\n\n### ⚠️ Known limitations\n* Hytale is experimental.\n* No `/jmenu` on Fabric, NeoForge, Forge, Hytale or the proxies (Spigot/Paper/Folia only).\n* The API is not on a Maven repository yet: use the attached jar."
		},
